# Build context is the repository root (docker build -f docker/Dockerfile .).
# Docker reads <context>/.dockerignore, or with BuildKit the per-Dockerfile
# file docker/Dockerfile.dockerignore — a symlink to this file, so the rules
# apply without touching the repository root. (Unverified on every builder:
# if yours ignores the symlink, the build still works, just with a larger
# context; the Dockerfile COPYs only the directories it needs.)
# Keep in step with docker/config-hash.sh, which skips the same litter.
.git
.gitignore
.venv
.venv-*
venv
wheels
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.egg-info
**/.DS_Store
**/._*
**/.pytest_cache
workspace
data
recording
configs/data
tests
docs
# ...except its PDFs: the instructor list ships two of them (downloads.yaml).
!docs/*.pdf
deploy
scripts
docker/*.env
!docker/*.env.example
